"""Nastas, reference fiche (v3, medium tier), PART A: Biography (Origins, Red Dead Redemption 1911 with the three
Act III missions in which he appears and the newspaper notice of his death, Undead Nightmare kept apart).

SOURCE REGISTER (Red Dead Wiki EN and FR, fetched Oct 2026; shared cache scripts/v3/work/_m/, copies in
scripts/v3/work/nastas/fc/):
- Character page "Nastas" (EN, nastas/en.txt: infobox, Background, Events of Red Dead Redemption, Events of Undead
  Nightmare, Murders Committed, Quotes, Trivia) and FR page "Nastas" (nastas/fr.txt: Histoire, Interactions,
  Anecdotes).
- Transcripts (primary for every scene told here): "Bear One Another's Burdens/dialogues", "At Home with
  Dutch/dialogues", "For Purely Scientific Purposes/dialogues".
- Mission pages: "Bear One Another's Burdens" (42nd mission, first of West Elizabeth; bag over his head; John
  carries him; Ross's car; office of MacDougal), "At Home with Dutch" (44th; miner who cuts his arm; dynamite cart;
  three men outside the cave; the scout Helaku; Dutch's shot hits the binoculars), "For Purely Scientific Purposes"
  (45th; Bearclaw Camp; Enepay, Kosumi, Hinto; casualties list), "Curious Tales from Blackwater" (Undead Nightmare;
  no dialogue page exists), "Undead Nightmare" (story summary and "Canonical Differences").
- In-game newspaper (primary text): Blackwater Ledger No. 59, available after "The Prodigal Son Returns (To Yale)",
  Miscellany column. The wiki page of this issue is empty; the text is taken from the ireddead.com newspaper guide
  (fetched 21 Oct 2026; full text in scripts/v3/work/reyes/fc/ireddead_newspapers.html, Miscellany of No. 59; the
  copy nastas/fc/ireddead_Ledger_No59_text.txt is truncated), verbatim: "Nastas (Surname Unknown), of
  Indian descent, has passed away at Bear Claw Cabin in Tall Trees. May you find God, my dear friend. Prof. Harold
  MacDougal Esq."
- Cross-checked with the fact-checked parts edgar_A/B (Ross's lines in the car; "beaten and tied up"), john_B/C/D,
  dutch_B/C/D (At Home with Dutch: Dutch fires at John, the bullet hits the binoculars; Enepay, Hinto, Kosumi),
  and HOUSE_FACTS (Dutch lets himself fall from the cliff; Undead Nightmare never mixed with canon).

VERIFIED POINTS: the tip on the wreck came from the informant (Fordham: "That informant better not have been lying
to us", then "that's our informant. Nastas"; the mission page says Nastas gave the location); the transcript never
says that Nastas set the trap or knew of it. He was tied up and wounded: John tells MacDougal he was shot in the leg
and badly beaten (transcript). The miner in the cave: the transcript only says Nastas kills him; the cut to the arm
is the mission page's. Nastas carried John down from the cliffs (MacDougal first says "Nastas and I carried you
down", then credits Nastas alone). Enepay's words are "You shut your mouth, you treacherous snake!" (transcript;
the wiki pages paraphrase this as "traitor"). Nastas is shot in the head (transcript stage direction; the mission
page says forehead, the character page says face). John then kills Enepay, Kosumi and Hinto (transcript stage
direction). The notice of his death is in Ledger No. 59 (1911), NOT a 1914 paper as the FR wiki says.

EXCLUDED: the EN wiki's "it can be assumed" that he infiltrated the gang to rescue his tribesmen (speculation, the
page's own words); the FR wiki's claim that he is a former member of Dutch's gang who infiltrated it (no transcript
line, contradicts nothing but is unsourced); "classical English education at a boarding school" as fact (only "I
grew up on a reservation and attended school" is in the transcript; "boarding school" attributed); "Nastas has
arranged for Dutch to be present on the wreck for John to capture" (overstates the transcript); John "identifies"
or "sympathizes" with Nastas, "views him with respect" (wiki interpretation); "unconditionally accompanies him"
(interpretation); "an enraged John" (interpretation; John's line is quoted in part C); the bite-wound reading that
"hints" at an alternate timeline and the expansion page's "survived the attack" (both tie Undead Nightmare to the
canon death; only the wound is kept, attributed); the FR wiki's
1914 date for MacDougal's notice (contradicted by the newspaper's issue number); the FR wiki's "MacDougal is in
favour of civilization and says the rest is savagery" summary and Nastas's "he is a great man at heart" line (no
transcript line found); the live v2 fiche's claims (Nastas works for MacDougal as employee, identifies Dutch's
people, killed "before John reaches Cochinay", "moves freely between the two sides"): unsourced or wrong.

OWNERSHIP: lines most likely quoted in part B "In his own words" ("No, sir. I grew up on a reservation and attended
school.", "But we hunt to eat, not for sport.", "There is no respect for the land anymore.", "My people have
already endured many disasters. Before, this was all our land.", "For a wise man, you are a very stupid man,
mister.") are only paraphrased here. Names and pronunciations, appearance, weapons, horse and flute are in part B.
Mission rewards, achievements and mission trivia are in part C. The voice actor and cut content are in part D.
Undead Nightmare is kept in its own h3.
"""


def two(en, fr): return {"en": en, "fr": fr}


BLOCKS = [
    # ================================================================ Origins
    {"h3": two("Origins", "Origines"), "year": ""},
    {"p": two("Nastas is a Native American who lives in West Elizabeth in 1911. The games give no surname, no birth date and no tribe for him, and the notice published after his death gives no surname either (see below). What is known of his past comes from one exchange in Harold MacDougal's office. When the professor addresses him in mock metaphors, Nastas answers that he grew up on a reservation and went to school. According to the Red Dead Wiki, he was taught English at a boarding school.",
              "Nastas est un Amérindien qui vit dans l'État de West Elizabeth en 1911. Les jeux ne lui donnent ni nom de famille, ni date de naissance, ni tribu, et la brève parue après sa mort ne lui en donne pas davantage (voir plus bas). On ne sait de son passé que ce qu'il en dit lors d'un échange dans le bureau de Harold MacDougal. Quand le professeur s'adresse à lui par de pseudo-métaphores, Nastas répond qu'il a grandi dans une réserve et qu'il est allé à l'école. Le Red Dead Wiki précise que c'est dans un pensionnat qu'il a appris l'anglais.")},
    {"p": two("When John Marston arrives in West Elizabeth, Nastas is an informant for the Bureau of Investigation, whose agents [[edgar-ross|Edgar Ross]] and [[archer-fordham|Archer Fordham]] work from Blackwater. The games never show how he came to work for them. On the wreck of the Serendipity, Fordham calls him their informant, and the mission page of \"Bear One Another's Burdens\" says he is the source who gave the agents Dutch's supposed location.",
              "Quand John Marston arrive dans l'État de West Elizabeth, Nastas est informateur du Bureau of Investigation, dont les agents [[edgar-ross|Edgar Ross]] et [[archer-fordham|Archer Fordham]] opèrent depuis Blackwater. Les jeux ne montrent jamais comment il en est venu à travailler pour eux. Sur l'épave du Serendipity, Fordham le présente comme leur informateur, et la page de la mission \"Bear One Another's Burdens\" précise que c'est lui qui a fourni aux agents la cachette supposée de Dutch.")},

    # ================================================================ RDR1 1911
    {"h3": two("Red Dead Redemption (1911)", "Red Dead Redemption (1911)"), "year": "1911"},
    {"p": two("In 1911, the Bureau holds [[john-marston|John Marston]]'s wife and son until he has delivered the members of his old gang. After [[bill-williamson|Bill Williamson]] and [[javier-escuella|Javier Escuella]], the last target is [[dutch-van-der-linde|Dutch van der Linde]], who has formed a new gang in West Elizabeth. Nastas appears in three missions of Red Dead Redemption, all at the start of the third act: \"Bear One Another's Burdens\", \"At Home with Dutch\" and \"For Purely Scientific Purposes\". He is killed in the last of them.",
              "En 1911, le Bureau retient la femme et le fils de [[john-marston|John Marston]] jusqu'à ce qu'il lui ait livré les membres de son ancienne bande. Après [[bill-williamson|Bill Williamson]] et [[javier-escuella|Javier Escuella]], la dernière cible est [[dutch-van-der-linde|Dutch van der Linde]], qui a formé une nouvelle bande dans l'État de West Elizabeth. Nastas apparaît dans trois missions de Red Dead Redemption, toutes au début du troisième acte : \"Bear One Another's Burdens\", \"At Home with Dutch\" et \"For Purely Scientific Purposes\". Il est tué dans la dernière.")},

    {"h4": two("Act III: West Elizabeth", "Acte III : West Elizabeth"), "chapter": "A3"},
    {"p": two("In \"Bear One Another's Burdens\", Ross tells John in Blackwater that the Bureau knows where Dutch is. Fordham says Dutch is believed to be holed up with a group of renegades near the wreck of the Serendipity, a riverboat. The three men drive there in the agents' automobile, Fordham at the wheel. Ross stays with the car on the cliff while John and Fordham go down on foot. The wreck is quiet, and Fordham says the informant had better not have lied to them. John follows the shouts to an upper deck and finds a man tied up, with a bag over his head according to the mission page. Fordham recognizes Nastas, who warns them that it is a trap. Dutch's men then surround them.",
              "Dans \"Bear One Another's Burdens\", Ross annonce à John, à Blackwater, que le Bureau sait où se trouve Dutch. D'après Fordham, il se terre avec une bande de renégats près de l'épave du Serendipity, un ancien bateau à aubes. Les trois hommes s'y rendent dans l'automobile des agents, Fordham au volant. Ross reste près de la voiture, sur la falaise, pendant que John et Fordham descendent à pied. L'épave est silencieuse, et Fordham lâche que l'informateur a intérêt à ne pas leur avoir menti. John suit des cris jusqu'à un pont supérieur et y trouve un homme ligoté, un sac sur la tête selon la page de la mission. Fordham reconnaît Nastas, qui les prévient qu'il s'agit d'un piège. Les hommes de Dutch les encerclent aussitôt.")},
    {"p": two("Fordham judges that Nastas cannot walk and orders John to carry him. John fights his way back to the car with Nastas on his shoulder, shooting with one hand. Ross has him laid on the back seat and asks who he is and whether he is a prisoner; Fordham answers that he is the informant and that he speaks English. On the road back, the engine fails and riders from Dutch's gang attack. Ross says they must get the man to a doctor, and holds the riders off with John while Fordham repairs the car. On the drive back, Ross decides to take him to [[harold-macdougal|Harold MacDougal]], an anthropologist who helps the agents deal with the Native population, to see what he can learn from him. John tells MacDougal that Nastas has been shot in the leg and badly beaten, and Fordham promises to send a doctor.",
              "Fordham estime que Nastas est incapable de marcher et ordonne à John de le porter. John regagne la voiture sous les balles, Nastas sur l'épaule, en tirant d'une main. Ross le fait installer sur la banquette arrière et demande qui il est, et s'il s'agit d'un prisonnier ; Fordham répond que c'est l'informateur et qu'il parle anglais. Sur le chemin du retour, le moteur lâche et des cavaliers de la bande de Dutch attaquent. Ross rappelle qu'il faut conduire l'homme chez un médecin, et repousse les cavaliers avec John pendant que Fordham répare la voiture. Sur la route du retour, Ross décide de le confier à [[harold-macdougal|Harold MacDougal]], un anthropologue qui aide les agents dans leurs rapports avec la population amérindienne, pour voir ce qu'il pourra en tirer. John explique au professeur que Nastas a reçu une balle dans la jambe et a été sérieusement passé à tabac, et Fordham promet d'envoyer un médecin.")},
    {"p": two("\"At Home with Dutch\" opens in MacDougal's office, where the professor has just told John that the blood of natives and of white men looks exactly the same under his microscope. Nastas walks in. MacDougal speaks to him in mock metaphors, then turns to John and explains that \"savages\" must be addressed simply; Nastas corrects him. He says he can show them where the bandits they are looking for are hiding: Dutch has drawn young men from the reservation, who are turning to bad things, and he is based in the hills at Cochinay. Nastas knows an unguarded way in, brings the horses round and leads the ride.",
              "\"At Home with Dutch\" s'ouvre dans le bureau de MacDougal, où le professeur vient d'expliquer à John qu'au microscope le sang des Amérindiens et celui des Blancs sont rigoureusement identiques. Nastas entre. MacDougal lui parle par pseudo-métaphores, puis se tourne vers John pour lui expliquer qu'il faut s'adresser simplement aux \"sauvages\" ; Nastas le reprend. Il propose de leur montrer où se cachent les bandits qu'ils recherchent : Dutch a attiré de jeunes hommes de la réserve, qui tournent mal, et il est installé dans les collines de Cochinay. Nastas connaît un chemin non gardé, amène les chevaux et ouvre la route.")},
    {"p": two("If the player has not yet unlocked the Manifest Destiny achievement, the three riders pass hunters shooting buffalo on the plains. MacDougal admires the animals; Nastas says the white man will soon wipe them out through overhunting, and that his people hunt to eat, not for sport. MacDougal replies that extinction is a myth refuted by Darwin and that hunting will make the buffalo stronger. In the forest of Tall Trees, Nastas tells MacDougal to enjoy the trees while he can, because they will soon be cut down, and complains that the land is no longer respected. When the professor asks him to talk through this \"primal emotion\", Nastas tells him not to worry about it.",
              "Si le joueur n'a pas encore débloqué le succès Manifest Destiny, les trois cavaliers croisent dans la plaine des chasseurs qui abattent des bisons. MacDougal admire les bêtes ; Nastas prédit que l'homme blanc les fera bientôt disparaître à force de les chasser, et rappelle que les siens chassent pour se nourrir, pas pour le plaisir. MacDougal rétorque que l'extinction est un mythe réfuté par Darwin et que la chasse rendra les bisons plus forts. Dans la forêt de Tall Trees, Nastas invite MacDougal à profiter des arbres tant qu'il le peut, car ils seront bientôt abattus, et déplore que plus personne ne respecte la terre. Quand le professeur lui demande de mettre des mots sur cette \"émotion primitive\", Nastas lui répond de ne pas s'en soucier.")},
    {"p": two("At the foot of the cliffs, MacDougal says he has no head for heights and rides back to Blackwater. Nastas and John leave the horses and climb. A wooden scaffold breaks under John, and Nastas tells him to find another route while he looks around. The two meet again and Nastas leads John into an old mine shaft. A miner attacks them inside; according to the mission page he cuts Nastas in the arm before Nastas kills him. A cart loaded with dynamite then rolls into the tunnel, and the mission page says three men are waiting outside when the pair escape. Nastas says he is badly hurt. He refuses to slow John down and tells him to go on, saying he will catch up or meet him on the way down.",
              "Au pied des falaises, MacDougal avoue qu'il n'a pas la tête aux hauteurs et rentre à Blackwater. Nastas et John laissent les chevaux et grimpent. Un échafaudage de bois cède sous John, et Nastas lui dit de chercher un autre passage pendant qu'il fait le tour. Une fois réunis, Nastas entraîne John dans une ancienne galerie de mine. Un mineur les attaque à l'intérieur ; d'après la page de la mission, il entaille le bras de Nastas avant que celui-ci ne le tue. Un wagonnet chargé de dynamite dévale alors le tunnel, et toujours selon la page de la mission, trois hommes les attendent à la sortie. Nastas se dit gravement blessé. Pour ne pas ralentir John, il l'envoie devant et promet de le rattraper ou de le retrouver à la descente.")},
    {"p": two("John climbs alone, silently kills or hogties the scout Helaku and takes his binoculars. Through them he watches Dutch's camp at Cochinay, until Dutch spots him and fires; the bullet hits the binoculars and John falls backwards, knocked out. He wakes in MacDougal's office in Blackwater. MacDougal first says that Nastas and he carried John down, then admits that Nastas heard the shots, climbed up to rescue John and carried him down, while he himself only improvised the escape plan. Nastas says that friends of his are with Dutch. MacDougal wants to reason with the Native members of the gang and save them from disaster; Nastas answers that his people have already lived through many disasters and that all this land was once theirs.",
              "John grimpe seul, tue ou ligote sans bruit l'éclaireur Helaku et lui prend ses jumelles. Il observe le camp de Dutch à Cochinay jusqu'à ce que Dutch le repère et tire : la balle frappe les jumelles, et John bascule en arrière, assommé. Il se réveille dans le bureau de MacDougal, à Blackwater. Le professeur affirme d'abord que Nastas et lui l'ont redescendu, puis reconnaît que c'est Nastas qui a entendu les coups de feu, est monté le secourir et l'a porté jusqu'en bas, lui-même s'étant contenté d'improviser le plan de repli. Nastas confie que des amis à lui sont avec Dutch. MacDougal veut raisonner les Amérindiens de la bande et leur éviter le désastre ; Nastas répond que les siens ont déjà traversé bien des désastres et que toute cette terre était autrefois la leur.")},
    {"p": two("MacDougal answers that his people have brought them civilization, and tells the story of a Yale acquaintance whose father once shot eighteen Natives in an afternoon in Wyoming. Nastas tells him that for a wise man he is very stupid. John leaves the two men to work out right from wrong. MacDougal calls Nastas simple-minded, then backs down as Nastas steps towards him.",
              "MacDougal lui oppose que les Blancs leur ont apporté la civilisation, et raconte l'histoire d'une connaissance de Yale dont le père aurait abattu dix-huit Amérindiens en un après-midi, dans le Wyoming. Nastas lui lance que, pour un sage, il est bien stupide. John laisse les deux hommes démêler seuls le bien du mal. MacDougal traite Nastas d'esprit simple, puis se ravise quand celui-ci s'avance vers lui.")},
    {"p": two("In \"For Purely Scientific Purposes\", MacDougal tells John that Nastas has set up a meeting, which the professor calls a pow-wow between Natives and whites, academics and criminals. Nastas, waiting with the horses, explains that some of Dutch's men have agreed to meet the professor at the Bear Claw cabin, in Tall Trees, and says they are curious to hear what a white man has concluded about their culture from the comfort of his hotel room. He advises MacDougal against asking them for skin samples from the soles of their feet. MacDougal says he is relieved to have the two men with him, Nastas above all. On the way, a grizzly bear crosses the road; MacDougal opens fire, and he and John kill it. Nastas remarks that the bear showed no aggression and would probably have moved on if they had not shot first.",
              "Dans \"For Purely Scientific Purposes\", MacDougal annonce à John que Nastas a organisé une rencontre, une sorte de palabre, selon le professeur, entre Amérindiens et Blancs, universitaires et hors-la-loi. Nastas, qui les attend avec les chevaux, explique que quelques hommes de Dutch ont accepté de rencontrer le professeur à la cabane de Bear Claw, dans Tall Trees, et ajoute qu'ils sont curieux de savoir ce qu'un Blanc a pu conclure de leur culture sans quitter le confort de sa chambre d'hôtel. Il déconseille à MacDougal de leur demander des échantillons de peau de la plante des pieds. Le professeur se dit soulagé de les avoir tous les deux à ses côtés, Nastas surtout. En route, un grizzly traverse le chemin ; MacDougal ouvre le feu, et John et lui abattent la bête. Nastas fait remarquer que l'ours ne montrait aucun signe d'agressivité et serait sans doute reparti s'ils n'avaient pas tiré les premiers.")},
    {"p": two("Three of Dutch's men are waiting in the cabin: Enepay, Kosumi and Hinto, as the Red Dead Wiki names them. MacDougal says they come in peace. Enepay answers that such words mean nothing from people like them, who have left his people living like animals in the dirt, and orders them to raise their hands; Kosumi demands their weapons. Nastas protests that this is not what was agreed. Enepay calls him a treacherous snake and shoots him in the head, killing him. John kills Enepay, Kosumi and Hinto, then fights off the rest of the gang around the cabin and escorts MacDougal back to Blackwater through further attacks. On the ride, MacDougal says that his studies, Nastas and the blood samples had led him to believe acculturation was possible, and that he could not have been more wrong.",
              "Trois hommes de Dutch attendent dans la cabane : Enepay, Kosumi et Hinto, selon les noms que leur donne le Red Dead Wiki. MacDougal assure qu'ils viennent en paix. Enepay répond que ces mots ne valent rien dans la bouche de gens comme eux, qui ont réduit les siens à vivre comme des bêtes dans la poussière, et leur ordonne de lever les mains ; Kosumi exige leurs armes. Nastas proteste que ce n'était pas ce qui était convenu. Enepay le traite de serpent perfide et l'abat d'une balle dans la tête. John tue Enepay, Kosumi et Hinto, repousse le reste de la bande autour de la cabane, puis raccompagne MacDougal jusqu'à Blackwater malgré de nouvelles attaques. En chemin, le professeur reconnaît que ses travaux, Nastas et les échantillons de sang l'avaient amené à croire l'acculturation possible, et qu'il n'aurait pas pu se tromper davantage.")},
    {"p": two("Issue No. 59 of the Blackwater Ledger goes on sale after the next mission of the strand, \"The Prodigal Son Returns (To Yale)\". Its Miscellany column carries a notice signed by the professor: \"Nastas (Surname Unknown), of Indian descent, has passed away at Bear Claw Cabin in Tall Trees. May you find God, my dear friend. Prof. Harold MacDougal Esq.\"",
              "Le numéro 59 du Blackwater Ledger est mis en vente après la mission suivante de la série, \"The Prodigal Son Returns (To Yale)\". Sa rubrique Miscellany publie une brève signée du professeur : \"Nastas (Surname Unknown), of Indian descent, has passed away at Bear Claw Cabin in Tall Trees. May you find God, my dear friend. Prof. Harold MacDougal Esq.\" (Nastas, nom de famille inconnu, d'ascendance indienne, s'est éteint à la cabane de Bear Claw, dans Tall Trees. Puissiez-vous trouver Dieu, mon cher ami. Professeur Harold MacDougal).")},

    # ================================================================ Undead Nightmare
    {"h3": two("Undead Nightmare (non-canon)", "Undead Nightmare (hors canon)"), "year": ""},
    {"p": two("Undead Nightmare, an expansion released in October 2010, is not part of the series' canon. Nastas appears in one of its missions, \"Curious Tales from Blackwater\", as one of the undead. John finds MacDougal alone in a deserted Blackwater, who says he has come back to do more research. The professor goes down an alley to fetch his medical bag; according to the mission page, he says he left his things with Nastas. An undead Nastas attacks him there and devours him. The mission then asks the player to kill or avoid Nastas, MacDougal and the other undead. According to the mission page, if the player spares them, the two can be met again later in the town or near the cemetery.",
              "Undead Nightmare, une extension sortie en octobre 2010, ne fait pas partie du canon de la série. Nastas apparaît dans l'une de ses missions, \"Curious Tales from Blackwater\", en mort-vivant. John trouve MacDougal seul dans un Blackwater désert, qui dit être revenu pour poursuivre ses recherches. Le professeur s'engage dans une ruelle pour récupérer sa trousse de médecin ; d'après la page de la mission, il dit avoir laissé ses affaires à Nastas. Nastas, devenu mort-vivant, se jette sur lui et le dévore. La mission demande ensuite au joueur de tuer ou d'éviter Nastas, MacDougal et les autres morts-vivants. D'après la page de la mission, si le joueur les épargne, il peut les recroiser plus tard en ville ou près du cimetière.")},
    {"p": two("The undead Nastas bears a bite wound on the neck, according to the Red Dead Wiki.",
              "D'après le Red Dead Wiki, le Nastas mort-vivant porte une morsure au cou.")},
]
